<BaseLayout title="Visa Stay Days Calculator — Inclusive Date Planner" description="Calculate an inclusive last day from a verified day allowance. Keep visa validity, admission permission and calendar-month limits separate."><article class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-4 py-10"><h1 class="text-3xl font-bold mb-4">Visa Expiry Days Calculator</h1><p class="mb-8">Enter an allowance expressed in days. This planner counts the entry date as day one; the actual admission record and country rules take precedence.</p><VisaExpiryCalculator client:load /><section class="prose max-w-none mt-10"><h2>Use the correct allowance</h2><p>Read the visa, decision and admission record. A visa’s expiry date can be different from the date a particular stay must end. Do not turn “six months” into 180 days: calendar months have different lengths.</p><h2>How the arithmetic works</h2><p>For a day-based allowance, the calculated last day is entry date plus the allowance minus one. A one-day allowance on 1 June therefore ends on 1 June. The optional exit date is compared with that inclusive period.</p><h2>What the result cannot establish</h2><p>The tool does not check multiple-entry conditions, cumulative stay limits, previous visits, extensions or legal immigration status. For Schengen short stays, use the separate <a href="/tools/schengen-90-180-calculator/">rolling 90/180 calculator</a> and read the visa conditions too.</p><h2>If dates conflict</h2><p>Ask the responsible authority before the deadline. Do not assume a calculator creates permission to remain. Keep an accessible copy of your decision and admission record and confirm any proposed extension through the official route.</p></section></article></BaseLayout>
